1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,276
Welcome to Daily Brief.

2
00:00:02,226 --> 00:00:06,071
It's Monday, November 23rd, 2026.

3
00:00:06,071 --> 00:00:08,738
Three stories in about three minutes.

4
00:00:08,738 --> 00:00:12,916
First, the climate talks in Türkiye have ended without a deal.

5
00:00:12,916 --> 00:00:19,690
COP31 ran nearly two days past its deadline and still closed on Sunday with no overarching agreement.

6
00:00:19,690 --> 00:00:28,166
Negotiators from almost two hundred countries could not bridge the gap on how to pay for the transition, and on how quickly to phase out fossil fuels.

7
00:00:28,166 --> 00:00:35,833
Delegates did agree on a long list of technical items, but the headline number the summit was supposed to produce never materialised.

8
00:00:35,833 --> 00:00:39,000
Campaigners called the outcome a missed chance.

9
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:43,869
Officials pointed to the next round of talks and said the process is still alive.

10
00:00:43,869 --> 00:00:48,214
Second, a milestone in the business of artificial intelligence.

11
00:00:48,214 --> 00:00:55,940
Anthropic has completed the largest IPO in history, a listing that instantly makes it one of the most valuable companies in the world.

12
00:00:55,940 --> 00:01:02,154
The company behind the Claude models has turned a research lab into a public company in under five years.

13
00:01:02,154 --> 00:01:08,357
Investors piled in despite the fact that AI firms still burn enormous amounts of cash on computing.

14
00:01:08,357 --> 00:01:13,988
The bet is simple: whoever owns the model layer will take a slice of nearly every industry.

15
00:01:13,988 --> 00:01:18,750
Third, OpenAI says it is now using its own models to design chips.

16
00:01:18,750 --> 00:01:30,297
The company disclosed that an AI system it built helped optimise the core design of one of AMD's flagship GPUs, improving power, performance and area by up to fourteen percent.

17
00:01:30,297 --> 00:01:35,047
Some of those changes have already gone into the files sent for manufacturing.

18
00:01:35,047 --> 00:01:42,833
That is a small number next to a headline, but it points somewhere interesting: AI being used to build the hardware that runs AI.

19
00:01:42,833 --> 00:01:45,059
That's your briefing for today.

20
00:01:45,059 --> 00:01:47,916
The full transcript is in the show notes.

21
00:01:47,916 --> 00:01:50,130
I'll be back tomorrow morning.

